course: dictionary
lesson: 13271
title: Goofy: silly, clumsy and fun
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Goofy is an informal word. It usually means silly, clumsy and funny in a harmless way, the kind of silliness that makes people smile rather than upset. «Grandad did a goofy dance in the kitchen, and we all laughed.» The clues show it is fun: nobody is hurt, and everyone is laughing together.
explain: Goofy can also describe a face. «Ben gave a goofy grin, with his big front teeth sticking out.» Here goofy means a silly, happy look. Ask yourself: what word would fit? Silly would fit, so goofy is close in meaning to silly.
explain: Goofy is also a name. With a capital G, it is the tall, clumsy Disney cartoon dog. «Goofy tripped over the garden hose again!» The capital letter is a clue that this is a name, not a describing word.
explain: In surfing and skateboarding, goofy tells you which foot is at the front. A rider who puts the right foot forward is goofy-footed. «Sam is goofy-footed, so he rides with his right foot forward.» This is a special meaning, so the words around it are the clue.
fact: Goofy means silly, clumsy and funny in a harmless way.
fact: «A goofy grin» means a silly, happy smile, often with big front teeth showing.
fact: Goofy with a capital G is the name of the Disney cartoon dog.
fact: In surfing and skateboarding, goofy-footed means riding with the right foot forward.
fact: Goofy is informal, so you use it in chat and stories, not in formal writing.
exercise: «Mum did a goofy dance when the song came on.» What does goofy mean here? | *Silly and funny in a harmless way | Very expensive | Angry and loud | Tired and slow
exercise: «Ben gave a goofy grin.» What does goofy describe? | *A silly, happy smile | A sad, wet face | A tall tree | A loud shout
exercise: Ella says Goofy is a cat. Who is Goofy? | *A tall, clumsy Disney cartoon dog | A kind of petrol station | A silly face made by a baby | A surfing board
test: «Sam is goofy-footed, so he rides his board with his right foot forward.» What does goofy-footed mean in surfing? | Not riding at all | Riding with the left foot forward | Falling off the wave | *Riding with the right foot forward
test: Why does Goofy have a capital G in «Goofy tripped over the rope»? | It is at the start of a sentence, so it must be a capital | It is a very important word | *It is the name of a character | It means the rope is goofy
exam: Which sentence uses Goofy as a name? | *«Goofy chased the ball across the lawn.» | «The goofy grin spread across his face.» | «The goofy surfer caught a big wave.» | «Her goofy dance made us giggle.»
